{"id":"amable","es":"amable","en":["kind"],"pos":"adjective","topic":"describing","note":"Same form for a man or a woman. muy amable is the usual thanks for a favour.","sent":{"es":"Muy {amable}, gracias.","en":"That is very kind, thank you."}}
{"id":"simpatico","es":"simpático","en":["nice","friendly"],"pos":"adjective","topic":"describing","note":"For people: pleasant company. Not sympathetic.","sent":{"es":"Tu hermano es muy {simpático}.","en":"Your brother is very nice."}}
{"id":"antipatico","es":"antipático","en":["unfriendly","unpleasant"],"pos":"adjective","topic":"describing","sent":{"es":"El vecino es un poco {antipático}.","en":"The neighbour is a bit unfriendly."}}
